WEBVTT

00:04:59.556 --> 00:05:01.236
to achieve the scale necessary.

00:05:02.356 --> 00:05:04.156
But the point here is really simple:

00:05:04.196 --> 00:05:09.156
it's that in today's terminology,
zero is not always zero.

00:05:09.676 --> 00:05:11.676
It depends on your definition.

00:05:12.236 --> 00:05:13.716
And that is a problem.

00:05:14.636 --> 00:05:18.916
And it's a problem that brings us
to the second bug in our net-zero program:

00:05:18.916 --> 00:05:20.196
problems with measurement,

00:05:20.236 --> 00:05:21.676
and specifically,

00:05:21.716 --> 00:05:24.516
problems with the way
that we do or don't measure

00:05:24.516 --> 00:05:27.236
the climate impacts
of different carbon offsets.

00:05:28.236 --> 00:05:31.476
Because not all offsets are created equal.